File: NAGtypes.info, Node: Top, Next: AbstractPoint, Up: (dir)

NAGtypes -- Common types used in Numerical Algebraic Geometry
*************************************************************

Description
===========

The package defines types used by the package *note NumericalAlgebraicGeometry:
(NumericalAlgebraicGeometry)Top, as well as other numerical algebraic geometry
packages: e.g., interface packages *note PHCpack: (PHCpack)Top, and
Bertini::Bertini.

Datatypes: 

  * *note Point: AbstractPoint, -- a numerical approximation of a point in a
    complex space
  * *note PolySystem: PolySystem, -- a polynomial system (usually with complex
    coefficients)
  * *note WitnessSet: WitnessSet, -- a witness set representing (possibly
    positive-dimensional) solution components
  * *note NumericalVariety: NumericalVariety, -- a numerical description of a
    variety
  * *note PolySpace: PolySpace, -- a polynomial vector subspace
  * *note DualSpace: DualSpace, -- a dual functional vector subspace

See the corresponding documentation nodes for description of provided service
functions.

We display the objects of all new types showing only partial data. Moreover, if
an object is assigned to a global variable, only the name of the variable is
shown. Use *note peek: (Macaulay2Doc)peek, for more information.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y]                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal((x^2+y^2+2)*x,(x^2+y^2+2)*y);                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : w1 = witnessSet(I , ideal(x-y), {point {{0.999999*ii,0.999999*ii}},     |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = w1                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : WitnessSet                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|point {{-1.000001*ii,-1.000001*ii}}} )                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : O = point {{0.,0.}}                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = O                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Point                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : numericalVariety {witnessSet(I, ideal R, {O}),w1}                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = a "numerical variety" with components in                                |
|     dim 0:  [dim=0,deg=1]-*may be reducible*-                               |
|     dim 1:  w1                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : NumericalVariety                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : V = oo                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = V                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : NumericalVariety                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : peek V                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = NumericalVariety{0 => {[dim=0,deg=1]-*may be reducible*-}}              |
|                      1 => {w1}                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : peek w1                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o8 = WitnessSet{cache => CacheTable{...1...}        }                        |
|                Equations => {-3} | x3+xy2+2x |                              |
|                             {-3} | x2y+y3+2y |                              |
|                Points => {{.999999*ii, .999999*ii}}                         |
|                          {{-ii, -ii}              }                         |
|                Slice => | 1 -1 0 |                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : peek O                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o9 = Point{cache => CacheTable{}}                                            |
|           Coordinates => {0, 0}                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

