areEqual(DualSpace,DualSpace) -- approximate equality of dual spaces
********************************************************************

  * Function: *note areEqual: areEqual,
  * Usage: 
        b = areEqual(A,B)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note DualSpace: DualSpace,, 
      * B, an instance of the type *note DualSpace: DualSpace,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Projective: areEqual, => ..., default value false, determine if
        solutions are equal
      * *note Tolerance: sortSolutions_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmTolerance=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value .000001, the tolerance of a numerical computation
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Two dual spaces are approximately equal if the have (approximately) the same
base *note point(DualSpace): DualSpace, and the linear spaces spanned by the
differential operators are equal approximately.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = dualSpace(matrix{{y^2,x^2+x*y}},point{{1,1}})                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = | y2 x2+xy |                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : DualSpace                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : B = dualSpace(matrix{{x^2+x*y+y^2,y^2+0.00000001}},point{{1,1+0.00000001|
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | x2+xy+y2 y2+1e-8 |                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : DualSpace                                                               |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|}})                                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : b = areEqual(A,B)                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note areEqual(DualSpace,DualSpace): areEqual_lpDualSpace_cmDualSpace_rp,
    -- approximate equality of dual spaces
