components(NumericalVariety) -- list components of a numerical variety
**********************************************************************

  * Function: *note components: (Macaulay2Doc)components,
  * Usage: 
        components(V)
        components(V,a)
        components(V,a,b)
  * Inputs:
      * V, a *note numerical variety: NumericalVariety,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of *note witness sets: WitnessSet,

Description
===========

Returns a list of components of a numerical variety. If a (an *note integer:
(Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,) and/or b (an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ, or *note
infinity: (Macaulay2Doc)infinity,) are specified, then components of dimension
a (respectively, components of dimension at least a and at most b) are
returned.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y]; I = ideal((x^2+y^2+2)*x,(x^2+y^2+2)*y);                    |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : w1 := witnessSet(I , ideal(x-y), {point {{0.999999*ii,0.999999*ii}},    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = [dim=1,deg=2]-*may be reducible*-                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : WitnessSet                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|point {{-1.000001*ii,-1.000001*ii}}} )                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : w0 := witnessSet(I, ideal R, {point {{0.,0.}}})                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = [dim=0,deg=1]-*may be reducible*-                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : WitnessSet                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : V := numericalVariety {w0,w1}                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = a "numerical variety" with components in                                |
|     dim 0:  [dim=0,deg=1]-*may be reducible*-                               |
|     dim 1:  [dim=1,deg=2]-*may be reducible*-                               |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : NumericalVariety                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : components V                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o6 = {[dim=0,deg=1]-*may be reducible*-, [dim=1,deg=2]-*may be reducible*-}  |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note NumericalVariety: NumericalVariety, -- a numerical variety

Ways to use this method:
