isGEQ -- compare two points
***************************

  * Usage: 
        b = isGEQ(x,y)
  * Inputs:
      * x, a *note point: AbstractPoint,or a list of complex (floating point)
        numbers
      * y, a *note point: AbstractPoint,or a list of complex (floating point)
        numbers
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Tolerance: sortSolutions_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmTolerance=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value .000001, the tolerance of a numerical computation
  * Outputs:
      * b, tells if x is (approximately) greater or equal than y

Description
===========

The inputs are lists of complex numbers, the order is (approximately)
lexicographic: regard each complex n-vector as real 2n-vector, for the
corresponding coordinates a and b (of two real 2n-vectors) a < b if b-a is
larger than *note Tolerance: (NumericalLinearAlgebra)Tolerance,.

+---------------------------+
|i1 : isGEQ({1,1,1},{1,0,2})|
|                           |
|o1 = true                  |
+---------------------------+
|i2 : isGEQ({1,1e-7},{1, 0})|
|                           |
|o2 = true                  |
+---------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note areEqual: areEqual, -- determine if solutions are equal

