numericalVariety(List) -- construct a numerical variety
*******************************************************

  * Function: *note numericalVariety: numericalVariety_lpList_rp,
  * Usage: 
        V = numericalVariety Ws; V = projectiveNumericalVariety Ws; 
  * Inputs:
      * Ws, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, contains (projective) witness
        sets representing components of a variety
  * Outputs:
      * V, a *note numerical variety: NumericalVariety,

Description
===========

Constructs a numerical (affine or projective) variety. It is NOT expected that
every witness set W in the list Ws has the same W.Equations.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y]; I = ideal((x^2+y^2+2)*x,(x^2+y^2+2)*y);                    |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : w1 = witnessSet(I , ideal(x-y), {point {{0.999999*ii,0.999999*ii}},     |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = w1                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : WitnessSet                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|point {{-1.000001*ii,-1.000001*ii}}} )                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : w0 = witnessSet(I, ideal R, {point {{0.,0.}}})                          |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = w0                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : WitnessSet                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : V = numericalVariety {w0,w1}                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = V                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : NumericalVariety                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

