projectiveWitnessSet -- construct a ProjectiveWitnessSet
********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        w = projectiveWitnessSet(E,C,S,P)
  * Inputs:
      * E, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, in a polynomial ring over
        *note CC: (Macaulay2Doc)CC,
      * C, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, in a polynomial ring over
        *note CC: (Macaulay2Doc)CC,
      * S, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,,  complex coefficients of a
        linear system
      * P, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, contains witness points (of type
        *note AbstractPoint: AbstractPoint,)
  * Outputs:
      * w, an instance of the type *note ProjectiveWitnessSet:
        ProjectiveWitnessSet,

Description
===========

Used to construct a witness set for a component of the variety V(E).  An affine
chart is specified by the matrix of the coefficients of the (normalized) linear
equation defining the chart: e.g., ax+by+cz=1 is encoded as [a,b,c].

It is expected that the, V(E) and the plane V(S) defined by S are of
complementary dimensions and that P is contained in the intersection of V(E+C)
and V(S).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = CC[x,y,z]                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : w = projectiveWitnessSet( ideal(x^2+y^2+2*z^2), matrix{{0,0,1}},        |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = w                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : WitnessSet                                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|matrix{{1,-1,0}}, {point {{0.999999*ii,0.999999*ii,1.}}, point {{            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|-1.000001*ii,-1.000001*ii,1.}}} )                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : peek w                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = WitnessSet{AffineChart => | 0 0 1 |               }                     |
|                cache => CacheTable{...1...}                                 |
|                Points => {{.999999*ii, .999999*ii, 1}}                      |
|                          {{-ii, -ii, 1}              }                      |
|                Slice => | 1 -1 0 |                                          |
|                                    2    2     2                             |
|                Equations => ideal(x  + y  + 2z )                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use projectiveWitnessSet:
=================================

  * "projectiveWitnessSet(Ideal,Matrix,Matrix,List)"

For the programmer
==================

