solutionsWithMultiplicity -- replaces clusters of approximately equal points by single points with multiplicity
***************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = solutionsWithMultiplicity S
  * Inputs:
      * S, *note points: AbstractPoint,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Tolerance: sortSolutions_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmTolerance=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value .000001, the tolerance of a numerical computation
  * Outputs:
      * M, *note points: AbstractPoint, with a multiplicity field

Description
===========

Clusters the points and outputs a list with one point p per cluster with
p.*note Multiplicity: AbstractPoint, equal to the size of the cluster. If the
multiplicity is not 1, then p.*note SolutionStatus: AbstractPoint, is set to
*note Singular: AbstractPoint,; otherwise, it is inherited from one of the
points in the cluster.

Whether two points are approximately equal is decided by the function *note
areEqual: areEqual, that depends on *note Tolerance:
(NumericalLinearAlgebra)Tolerance,.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : a = point {{0,1}}                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = a                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Point                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : b = point {{0.000000001,1+0.00000000001*ii}}                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = b                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Point                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : c = point {{0.001*ii,1}}                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = c                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Point                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = solutionsWithMultiplicity {a,b,c}                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {a, c}                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : peek M                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {Point{cache => CacheTable{...1...}},                                   |
|            Coordinates => {0, 1}                                            |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     Point{cache => CacheTable{...1...}}}                                    |
|           Coordinates => {.001*ii, 1}                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

A point in a cluster may be farther than *note Tolerance:
(NumericalLinearAlgebra)Tolerance, from another point in the cluster. (In that
case there has to be another point in the cluster that is within the *note
