sortSolutions(List) -- sort the list of solutions
*************************************************

  * Function: *note sortSolutions: sortSolutions_lpList_rp,
  * Usage: 
        t = sortSolutions s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, contains solutions (represented
        either by lists of coordinates or *note points: AbstractPoint,)
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Tolerance: sortSolutions_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmTolerance=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => ..., default value .000001, the tolerance of a numerical computation
      * Weights => ..., default value null
  * Outputs:
      * t, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, contains solutions sorted as
        described below

Description
===========

The sorting is done lexicographically regarding each complex n-vector as real
2n-vector. The output format of *note track:
(NumericalAlgebraicGeometry)track_lpList_cmList_cmList_rp, and *note
solveSystem: (NumericalAlgebraicGeometry)solveSystem_lpList_rp, is respected.
For the corresponding coordinates a and b (of two real 2n-vectors) a < b if b-a
is larger than *note Tolerance: (NumericalLinearAlgebra)Tolerance,.


+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : needsPackage "NumericalAlgebraicGeometry"                               |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = NumericalAlgebraicGeometry                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Package                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = CC[x,y];                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : s = solveSystem {x^2+y^2-1, x*y}                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{1, 8.30314e-21+4.44918e-20*ii}, {3.02251e-20+2.05294e-20*ii, -1},     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {-3.02251e-20-2.05294e-20*ii, 1}, {-1, -8.30314e-21-4.44918e-20*ii}}    |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : sortSolutions s                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = {{-1, -8.30314e-21-4.44918e-20*ii}, {3.02251e-20+2.05294e-20*ii, -1},   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     {-3.02251e-20-2.05294e-20*ii, 1}, {1, 8.30314e-21+4.44918e-20*ii}}      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The sorting described above does not possess good properties, since there may
be near ties in specific coordinate values between several points. A better way
is to specify a random weight (of length 2n where n=#points) as an optional
parameter *note sortSolutions(...,Weights=>...): sortSolutions_lpList_rp,,
which provides a linear functional that evaluates to distinct (and
sufficiently) real numbers on the given points.

See also
========

  * *note solveSystem: (NumericalAlgebraicGeometry)solveSystem_lpList_rp, --
    solve a system of polynomial equations
  * *note track: (NumericalAlgebraicGeometry)track_lpList_cmList_cmList_rp, --
    track a linear segment homotopy given start and target system
  * *note areEqual: areEqual, -- determine if solutions are equal

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note sortSolutions(List): sortSolutions_lpList_rp, -- sort the list of
    solutions
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

