WitnessSet -- a witness set
***************************

Description
===========

This type stores a witness set of an equidimensional solution component. The
following methods can be used to access a *note WitnessSet: WitnessSet,:
  * ideal -- get the defining ideal of the algebraic superset
  * equations -- get the list of defining polynomials of the algebraic superset
  * slice -- get linear functions defining the slicing plane
  * points -- get the list of witness points (which are zeroes of all above)
Also one may determine
  * dim -- the dimension
  * codim -- the codimension
  * deg -- the degree (the number of witness points)
  * ring -- the ring of the defining polynomials
Only dimension and degree are displayed (by *note net: (Macaulay2Doc)net,); to
see the data stored in a witness set use *note peek: (Macaulay2Doc)peek,.

For developers:
===============

Required keys in a *note WitnessSet: WitnessSet, are
  * Equations -- an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,
  * Slice -- a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List, or a *note matrix:
    (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,
  * Points--  a list of *note points: AbstractPoint,
  * cache.IsIrreducible -- takes values *note null: (Macaulay2Doc)null,(not
    determined), *note true: (Macaulay2Doc)true,, or *note false:
    (Macaulay2Doc)false,
Optional keys:
  * ProjectionDimension -- an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the witness set
    describes a lifted variety (its projection on the first ProjectionDimension
    coordinates is the variety the witness set represents)

See also
========

  * *note witnessSet: witnessSet, -- construct a WitnessSet
  * *note ProjectiveWitnessSet: ProjectiveWitnessSet, -- a projective witness
    set
  * *note NumericalVariety: NumericalVariety, -- a numerical variety
  * *note declareIrreducible: declareIrreducible, -- declares a component
    represented by the witness set irreducible

